  "term": "agnosia",
  "definition": "Agnosia is a loss of the ability to recognize or understand the meaning of sensory information even though the basic senses themselves are still working. For example, a person with tactile agnosia cannot identify an object by touch alone despite normal basic touch and position sensation.",
